[Desktop Entry]
# Local override of /usr/share/applications/org.kde.dolphin.desktop.
#
# Purpose: theme Dolphin from the palette, via GTK rather than via qt6ct.
#
# SUPERSEDED 2026-08-19 -- kept only because removing it is a separate change.
# KDE apps are now themed by a real KDE color scheme
# (theme-src/templates/kde-colors.colors.in), and KColorSchemeManager sets the
# palette AFTER the platform theme, so Dolphin looks the same on gtk3 or on
# qt6ct. See README "System notes". The "measured and FAILED" list below is
# accurate about what was tried but WRONG in its conclusion: kdeglobals is not
# inert, it just holds a pointer -- `[UiSettings] ColorScheme` naming a
# .colors file in a scanned color-schemes/ directory -- not the colors
# themselves, and .colors wants decimal R,G,B rather than hex.
#
# conf/env.lua exports QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=qt6ct session-wide. That is right
# for pavucontrol-qt and wifi-qt but WRONG for Dolphin, so this file swaps the
# value to gtk3 for Dolphin alone. Qt's gtk3 platform theme (libqgtk3.so, part
# of qt6-base -- nothing extra installed) builds the QPalette from the GTK
# theme, and ~/.config/gtk-3.0/settings.ini is itself generated by theme-set.
# So Dolphin ends up on the SAME palette as everything else and follows
# `theme-set gruvbox` automatically, with no per-app color file to maintain.
#
# Why not the obvious routes -- all three were measured on this machine
# 2026-08-18, and all three FAILED, so do not retry them:
#   - qt6ct's own palette: never reaches Dolphin. Verified with the stylesheet
#     disabled in an isolated XDG_CONFIG_HOME, so QSS could not mask it.
#   - ~/.config/kdeglobals: inert. KConfig reads it back fine (kreadconfig6
#     returns the values), but nothing converts it to a QPalette.
#   - KDE's own /usr/share/color-schemes/BreezeDark.colors copied in verbatim:
#     still light. The component that applies KDE color schemes is
#     KDEPlatformTheme from plasma-integration, which drags in kwin and
#     plasma-workspace -- an entire second desktop, so it is not an option.
#
# A same-named file here shadows the system one entirely (XDG_DATA_HOME wins
# over /usr/share), so this file must carry every key that matters, not just
# the changed Exec. Localised Name/Comment strings are dropped deliberately;
# the English ones are what this system uses.
#
# To undo: delete this file, then run
#   update-desktop-database ~/.local/share/applications
Name=Dolphin
GenericName=File Manager
Comment=Manage your files
Exec=env QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=gtk3 dolphin %u
Icon=org.kde.dolphin
Type=Application
X-DocPath=dolphin/index.html
Categories=Qt;KDE;System;FileTools;FileManager;
MimeType=inode/directory;
InitialPreference=10
Keywords=files;file management;file browsing;samba;network shares;Explorer;Finder;
X-DBUS-ServiceName=org.kde.dolphin
X-KDE-Shortcuts=Meta+E
StartupWMClass=dolphin
